# What xwin 0.10.0 downloads from Microsoft for manifest_17.json: the
# package manifest of Visual Studio 17.14.41, then the C runtime 14.44
# and the Windows SDK 10.0.26100 for x86_64, desktop variant.
#
# Nothing of this is in the repository or in a container image. The fetch
# phase downloads it from Microsoft on the machine of whoever builds,
# once they have accepted the licence, and checks every file against
# this list. A missing file, an extra file or a different byte stops the
# build.
#
# xwin checks each package against the hash the package manifest gives,
# but it cannot check the package manifest itself: the hash the channel
# manifest gives for it is wrong, upstream says so. This list closes the
# gap. The recipe downloads that file itself and checks it before xwin
# reads it.
#
# To move to a newer release: replace manifest_17.json with
# https://aka.ms/vs/17/release/channel, run the fetch phase, and write
# this list again from /cache/microsoft/xwin/dl:
#   find . -type f ! -name manifest_17.json -printf '%P\0' | sort -z | xargs -0 sha256sum
